# What is wrong with a settings member's value: numbering, xref_format, the wire profiles, process_tag_scheme.
refusal-settings-issue-default = the default `{ $p0 }` names no scheme of `schemes`; tags would silently use the profile's default scheme
refusal-settings-issue-scheme-token = scheme `{ $p0 }`: format { $p1 } has the unknown token { $p2 }, which would print into tags; tokens are {"{"}letter{"}"}, {"{"}counter{"}"}, {"{"}subcounter{"}"}, {"{"}page{"}"}, {"{"}column{"}"}, {"{"}row{"}"}
refusal-settings-issue-scheme-unused = scheme `{ $p0 }` would not be applied ({ $p1 }); a scheme needs counter scope "page" and formats with {"{"}page{"}"}, {"{"}letter{"}"} and {"{"}counter{"}"}
refusal-settings-issue-counter-scope = its counter scope is not "page"
refusal-settings-issue-no-page = its format has no {"{"}page{"}"} token
